# /etc/conf.d/llama-mon - configuration for the llama.cpp monitor service.
# Installed by local/openrc/llama-mon-install.sh; an existing copy is never
# overwritten unless the installer is run with --force-conf. Changes take
# effect on the next "rc-service llama-mon restart".
#
# The monitor's main configuration is the JSON file
# /etc/llama-mon/config.json (seeded once by the installer; schema:
# local/monitor/README.md - GPU visibility, spot-price sources and the power
# throttle live only there). The MON_* variables below are OPTIONAL
# overrides: only ones uncommented here reach the monitor and win over the
# JSON file (precedence: built-in defaults < JSON file < environment).

# Checkout the monitor is launched from.
MON_REPO="@REPO@"

# Unix user the monitor runs as. Setting GPU power caps (the spot-price
# throttle) needs root, so keep it root unless you installed the sudoers
# drop-in (local/systemd/llama-mon.sudoers) for an unprivileged user.
MON_USER="root"

# Optional env overrides (uncomment to force values past the JSON config):
#MON_HOST="127.0.0.1"
#MON_PORT="8085"
# Base URLs of the llama-server instances to poll (space or comma separated;
# each must run with --metrics; Strata backends are auto-detected).
#MON_URLS="http://127.0.0.1:8080"
#MON_INTERVAL="2"
#MON_WINDOW="1800"
#MON_GPUS=""
# Alternative JSON config file path (default /etc/llama-mon/config.json).
#MON_CONFIG="/etc/llama-mon/config.json"
